# Same message with relaxed alignment (the default): the parent domain's signature aligns, DMARC passes.
client-ip: 198.51.100.9
helo: mail.example.com
mail-from: alice@elsewhere.example
authserv-id: mx.receiver.example
[zone]
elsewhere.example TXT v=spf1 ip4:198.51.100.9 -all
_dmarc.example.com TXT v=DMARC1; p=reject
[message]
From: Alice <alice@news.example.com>
To: Bob <bob@receiver.example>
Subject: Fixture
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Message-ID: <fx1@example.com>

Hello Bob.
[sign domain=example.com selector=s1]
[expect]
mx.receiver.example; spf=pass smtp.mailfrom=alice@elsewhere.example; dkim=pass (2048-bit key) header.d=example.com header.s=s1 header.b=Bs8HNz2w; dmarc=pass (p=REJECT sp=REJECT dis=NONE) header.from=news.example.com
